      "claim": "L8-PATTERNS",
      "verdict": "FAIL",
      "reason": "Pattern (d) occurs in the target headings at candidate/statement-ledger.md:992 and 2289 and their references at :60, :755 and :2345: 'whole result' is used despite one-mode-only coverage or supplied inputs (W2). The scoped 'nothing supplied' statements concern genuinely proved special cases and are not themselves false. No unsupported implicit side condition or totalized-arithmetic counterexample was found in the reviewed material."
    },
    {
      "claim": "CHANGED-ROW L:finite-word-cutoff",
      "verdict": "FAIL",
      "reason": "The merge replaces 'inputs-supplied' by 'same-assumptions' (prior/coverage-5ec3c11.yaml:263; diffs/coverage.diff:164-188; coverage.yaml:337). The added concrete theorem discharges the realization only for m_i = 1, not the arbitrary grouped modes of main TeX:2532-2538. Thus the concrete progress and new scope sentence are accurate, but the promoted assumption class is not (W1). The new TeX scope entry accurately mirrors the restricted scope."
